  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Douane beach is one of the small beaches and coves that extend L'Escalet towards Cap Taillat, on Ramatuelle's coastal path. It takes its name from the customs house standing right at the water's edge, built under Napoleon I and recently restored. Its white sand is among the most beautiful on the Côte d'Azur, with a direct panorama of Cap Taillat — Ramatuelle tourist office ranks it among the town's "most beautiful beaches".</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the 2025 "Dog friendly" leaflet of the Ramatuelle tourist office, all the town's beaches (Pampelonne, Bonne Terrasse, L'Escalet and the coves) are open to dogs on a leash. This leaflet mentions no period or time slot, and we did not find a municipal bylaw published online: if in doubt, call the tourist office (04 98 12 64 00). Swimming is allowed except in the zones reserved exclusively for swimming (ZRUB). La Douane beach is unsupervised (tourist office) and can only be reached on foot. As the Cap Taillat site is protected, stay on the waymarked paths and keep your dog on a leash (Conservatoire du littoral / CEN Paca).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: set off from L'Escalet car park and follow the coastal path (yellow waymarks); La Douane beach lies at the foot of the Cap Taillat peninsula, near the customs house. Bring water for your dog.</div>

      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <h3>Are dogs accepted at La Douane beach?</h3>
      <p>Yes, on a leash, according to Ramatuelle tourist office, as on the town's other beaches; the leaflet gives no dates or hours.</p>
      <h3>Is there a water point on site?</h3>
      <p>No water point is reported along the route by the sources consulted — remember to bring water for your dog.</p>
      <h3>How do I get to La Douane beach?</h3>
      <p>On foot only, via the coastal path, starting from L'Escalet beach car park (paid parking from 2 April to 4 October 2026).</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The path continues to <a href="/en/fiche-plage-cap-taillat">Cap Taillat</a>. For a more accessible beach, head for <a href="/en/fiche-pampelonne">Pampelonne beach</a> or <a href="/en/fiche-bonne-terrasse">Bonne Terrasse beach</a>. <a href="/en/fiche-escalet">L'Escalet beach</a>, a family beach of about 350 m (tourist office), is the starting point of the path.</p>
    </div>

